-- ======================================================= boot.rofl [boot] ===
-- The meta-kernel's own required results, stated in a comment block at the
-- foot of the file it governs. Seven assertions; START.md's Appendix A had
-- four, and the three added since are the interesting half.

duty[boot](b_malformed_empty, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "malformed[audit](R)   :- rule_known(R), not has_premise(R, _)").
duty[boot](b_breach_empty, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "breach[audit](R)      :- concludes(R, Rel), reserved(Rel)").
duty[boot](b_leak_empty, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "leak[audit](A,B)").
duty[boot](b_forged_empty, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "forged[audit](F)").
duty[boot](b_unmoded_empty, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "unmoded[audit](R)     :- uses_builtin(R, B), not mode(B, _)").
duty[boot](b_collected_declared_only, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "collected[audit](X)   :- collects_from(X, _)").
duty[boot](b_undefined_premise_empty, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "undefined_premise[audit](R, Rel) :- premise_pos(R, Rel)").
duty[boot](b_whynot_finite, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "whynot flows_to(red, blue)").
duty[boot](b_stratifiable_by_loading, guaranteed, "boot.rofl", "answered by the file LOADING AT ALL").

-- TWO REQUIRED RESULTS WERE WITHDRAWN, not merely re-anchored, and the
-- difference is the reason this ledger exists. `? unstratified(X) -> empty`
-- and `whynot unstratified(reach) -> finite demonstration via dep/reach` are
-- not sentences that moved: the ten rules that answered them left boot.rofl
-- when the evaluator started peeling its schedule off the decoded rules, and
-- the relation they were about does not exist. Re-anchoring either of them to
-- the paragraph that explains their removal would have made the model say the
-- obligation still stands and is still cited, which is the flattering lie the
-- `unfounded` audit exists to catch — so both were deleted and replaced:
--   `b_stratifiable_by_loading` is what answers the first question now (a
--   program whose peel stalls is refused before a query is possible, so the
--   file loading IS the answer), and
--   `b_whynot_finite` keeps its id and its meaning — a finite failure
--   demonstration through a RECURSIVE relation — asked of `flows_to`, the
--   transitive closure boot.rofl still carries.
-- `b_forged_empty` and `b_unmoded_empty` are new for a duller reason: the
-- required-results list always ran those audits and never listed them.

-- ======================= docs/time-and-continuity.md [decided] =============
-- Decisions taken this week that amend the contract. Each `amends` link below
-- names the sentence it replaces, and both ends are cited.

-- ============================ docs/port-surface.md [decided] ================
-- The other half of the surface gap, and the opposite verdict. Residency is
-- the port's alone by decision; explanation is owed BY the port, because a
-- store that cannot say which firing produced a fact is a table.
duty[decided](d_port_owes_why, guaranteed, "docs/port-surface.md", "`why` and `whynot` are REQUIRED of the port").
cited_check[map](c_port_explains, "rust/rofl/tests/explain.rs", "why_walks_the_derivation_to_its_axioms").
guards[map](c_port_explains, d_port_owes_why).

duty[decided](d_not_p_is_this_tick, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "is not derivable in the CURRENT TICK").
duty[decided](d_dep_graph_is_one_tick, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "the dependency graph is about ONE tick").
duty[decided](d_semiring_is_one_tick, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "the semiring fold is about one tick too").
duty[decided](d_next_in_body_rejected, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "is rejected by the parser, deliberately").
duty[decided](d_veto_belongs_inside, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "A veto the model can express belongs inside the model").
duty[decided](d_retain_ticks, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "keeps the current tick's provenance plus the").
duty[decided](d_retention_off_by_default, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "It is off unless asked for").
duty[decided](d_retention_conditional, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "Retention is conditional on whether the program reads its own provenance").
duty[decided](d_tick_records_budget, guaranteed, "docs/time-and-continuity.md", "a tick now records the budget it was evaluated with").

-- ==================== docs/performance-invariants.md [perf] ================
-- Only the invariants that are about THIS kernel. I3, I5 and I6 in that
-- section are measurements of the FIELD (Souffle, RecStep, DDlog) and oblige
-- nothing here, so they are not duties and are not listed.

duty[perf](p_p1_one_witness_per_derivation, guaranteed, "docs/performance-invariants.md", "Provenance costs one witness per distinct derivation").
duty[perf](p_p2_provenance_is_not_the_cost, guaranteed, "docs/performance-invariants.md", "the reason this engine is slow").
duty[perf](p_i1_insertion_order_is_the_cost, guaranteed, "docs/performance-invariants.md", "Insertion order, not the index, is the cost").
duty[perf](p_i2_self_audit_tracks_program_size, guaranteed, "docs/performance-invariants.md", "Self-audit cost tracks program size, not data size").

-- ====================== docs/three-valued-answers.md [wfs] =================

duty[wfs](t_alternating_fixpoint, guaranteed, "docs/three-valued-answers.md", "runs an alternating fixpoint instead of the").
duty[wfs](t_budget_emits_no_unknown, guaranteed, "docs/three-valued-answers.md", "row is emitted at all").
duty[wfs](t_stratum_table_survives, guaranteed, "docs/three-valued-answers.md", "It survives, untouched, on the evaluator that reads it").

-- @who librarian

-- ========================================================== the map [map] ==
-- Editorial links: which check stands behind which duty, which sentence
-- replaced which. Every check below is named exactly as it is written in the
-- tree; `scanners/spec.ts` looks each one up, and a rename breaks the link
-- loudly (`dangling[coverage]`) instead of quietly.

-- ---- checks, as cited -----------------------------------------------------

-- THE KERNEL GREP TEST AND ITS GATE ARE DELETED, 2026-09-10, by the owner's
-- decision, and the duties they guarded are RE-AIMED rather than dropped. The
-- check had no model of the language: 120 whitelisted words of which 72 were
-- host tokens, plus 39 hand-typed relation names against the tree's 1 168.
-- Fifteen commits widened it, not one because it caught anything, and it was
-- carrying `in_perspective` after the kernel deleted that relation.
--
-- What discharges the duties now is DERIVED and not typed: the second engine,
-- which is diffed byte for byte on `canonicalState()` over the whole corpus,
-- so a domain relation hardcoded into one host makes the two disagree; and
-- `test/vocabulary-doc.test.ts`, which since today reads the vocabulary off
-- the RUNNING kernel (`RESERVED`, `STR_ARITY`) rather than off a list.












-- BOTH OF THESE WERE STALE AND ONE OF THEM DANGLED. The jobs stopped running
-- `node --test` and `bun test` when the suite became one golden loop, so
-- `c_ci_bun` named a step that no longer existed -- and `s_two_runtimes` and
-- `s_done_ci_green` quietly lost their bun-side guard. Nothing said so for as
-- long as `npm run speccheck` was dead. The node label still RESOLVED while
-- naming a runner it had stopped using, which is the worse half: a citation
-- that is correct and describes nothing.
cited_check[map](c_ci_node, ".github/workflows/ci.yml", "goldens (node)").
cited_check[map](c_ci_bun, ".github/workflows/ci.yml", "goldens (bun)").
cited_check[map](c_ci_typecheck, ".github/workflows/ci.yml", "typecheck").

-- ---- the prohibitions, which had nothing behind them at all -------------
-- Eleven `prohibited` duties read `open_shortcut` on 2026-09-12, the day the
-- coverage model was first wired into a world and first ran since `test/` was
-- removed. A prohibition has ONE mechanical form -- write the forbidden thing
-- down and require a refusal -- and two of these now have it. The rest are
-- cited against checks that already existed and were never written down: the
-- census holds 139 checks against 4 citations, so the gap the report measures
-- is mostly a MISSING BIBLIOGRAPHY rather than missing instruments.
--
-- Each body below was READ before it was cited. `run_reports_partial` asserts
-- `partial && !quiescent`, a non-empty `hole`, and a control that the wall is
-- the budget; `excise_recomputes_rather_than_reading_the_witness` excises BOTH
-- supports of a two-support fact, separately, because which witness the store
-- records is not fixed by the semantics -- and carries a single-support control
-- so it cannot pass by removing nothing.
cited_check[map](c_w_async_reserved, "facts/goldens.rofl", "async_reserved").
cited_check[map](c_w_unstratifiable, "facts/goldens.rofl", "unstratifiable").
cited_check[map](c_w_budget_wall, "facts/goldens.rofl", "budget_wall").
cited_check[map](c_port_partial, "rust/rofl/tests/explain.rs", "run_reports_partial_rather_than_pretending_to_have_finished").
cited_check[map](c_port_canonical, "rust/rofl/tests/explain.rs", "fact_keys_narrows_by_relation_and_comes_back_in_canonical_order").
cited_check[map](c_port_excise, "rust/rofl/tests/explain.rs", "excise_recomputes_rather_than_reading_the_witness").

guards[map](c_w_async_reserved, s_async_reserved_rejected).
guards[map](c_w_unstratifiable, s_reject_unstratified).
-- TWO SHAPES OF NOT HANGING, because the duty is about both. A negation cycle
-- is the loop that never settles and the loader refuses it by noticing that a
-- round bought nothing; a budget wall is the search too large to finish and the
-- kernel records why it stopped. A check for only one of them would leave the
-- other spelling of the same prohibition unguarded.
guards[map](c_w_unstratifiable, s_never_hang).
guards[map](c_w_budget_wall, s_never_hang).
guards[map](c_w_budget_wall, s_budget_emits_hole).
guards[map](c_port_partial, s_budget_emits_hole).
guards[map](c_port_canonical, s_canonical_order).
guards[map](c_port_excise, s_excise_not_from_witness).

-- TWO THAT A GOLDEN CANNOT HOLD, and the reason is the same in both: a golden
-- compares ONE run of one world against its own pin, and these duties are
-- about two runs differing. `regardless of insertion order` needs the same
-- program loaded twice with its facts reversed and the two settled stores
-- compared to EACH OTHER; `Hardcoding any boot.rofl rule` needs the same
-- program settled with the pack and without it, and the audit present in one
-- and absent in the other. Neither question fits inside a world.
cited_check[map](c_port_shuffle, "rust/rofl/tests/explain.rs", "the_settled_world_is_the_same_whichever_order_the_facts_arrived_in").
cited_check[map](c_port_pack, "rust/rofl/tests/explain.rs", "the_audits_are_a_loaded_pack_and_not_a_property_of_the_engine").

guards[map](c_port_shuffle, s_determinism).
guards[map](c_port_shuffle, s_a_replay_shuffled).
guards[map](c_port_pack, s7_no_hardcoded_boot).
guards[map](c_port_pack, l_unchecked_without_boot).
guards[map](c_port_pack, s_reserved_rejected_at_load).

-- PROVENANCE, JOINED RATHER THAN PRINTED. A log string can be shown and cannot
-- be JOINED, so the world joins a firing's middle column against `rule` and
-- against `concludes` and gets rows -- three-way, inside the language, no host
-- help. Every head there projects the fact id away, because reading provenance
-- is self-feeding: a rule keeping F in its head fires on the row its own firing
-- emitted and the ids never repeat. That non-termination is what `emits on
-- every firing` MEANS seen from inside, and it is the reason the obvious probe
-- is not the one written.
cited_check[map](c_w_provenance, "facts/goldens.rofl", "provenance_relational").

guards[map](c_w_provenance, s_provenance_per_firing).
guards[map](c_w_provenance, p_p1_one_witness_per_derivation).

-- ---- accepted by name, because the observance is structural ---------------
-- THE LAST OF THE ELEVEN, AND THE OWNER'S CALL RATHER THAN A MEASUREMENT.
-- `Evaluator reading parsed clause objects` is the mechanical form of START.md's
-- prime directive, and the honest position is that it is already so by
-- construction: `src/engine.ts` line 2 says `The evaluator reads rules ONLY from
-- the reflected store (decodeRules)`, and the code agrees -- ONE assignment to
-- the rule set in the whole file, `this.rules = kept` at line 488, fed by
-- `decodeRules(this.store)` at 468. The port is the same shape:
-- `decode_rules(&mut self.h, &self.v, &mut self.store)` at `engine.rs:246`.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS NOT is a check. START.md says in as many words that the likely
-- failure mode is `a kernel that hardcodes semantics and passes tests anyway`,
-- and this acceptance does not close that -- it says a person looked at the one
-- call site and signed for it. A probe would have to change the store's rule
-- rows by a route the parser never took and watch the evaluation honour them;
-- it is not written, and `accepted` rather than `guards` is how the report
-- keeps saying so.
accepted[map](s7_no_clause_objects, "satisfied by construction: one call site, decodeRules(store), in both engines -- signed for by the owner 2026-09-12, not measured").

-- ---- what stands behind what ----------------------------------------------

guards[map](c_ci_bun, s_two_runtimes).
guards[map](c_ci_node, s_two_runtimes).

guards[map](c_ci_node, s_done_ci_green).
guards[map](c_ci_bun, s_done_ci_green).







-- ---- what changed ---------------------------------------------------------
-- The amendment that matters: LIMITS.md still says provenance is never
-- collected, and `retainTicks` collects it. Neither LIMITS.md nor README.md
-- mentions the window; the decision is recorded only in
-- docs/time-and-continuity.md.

amends[map](d_retain_ticks, l_frozen_never_collected).

-- THE TEN RULES, and what their deletion did to the contract. START.md §3.2
-- puts stratification in boot.rofl as data and keeps a checker out of the
-- kernel; `src/rounds.ts` peels the phase order off the decoded rules, so that
-- sentence is not kept as written and `s_no_stratification_checker` is amended
-- rather than qualified — it is CONTRADICTED, not narrowed, and nothing
-- mechanical can hold a sentence that is false.
--
-- `s_reject_unstratified` was written as an amendment here first, and the model
-- refused it: `r_unstratifiable_is_budgeted` already qualifies that duty, and
-- retiring a qualified obligation would have marked a live, tested duty as no
-- longer owed — the flattering direction this ledger's own note warns about,
-- caught by the check that every qualified duty is still live. The kernel does
-- still reject unstratifiable programs, on both evaluators; what changed is the
-- FORM of the diagnostic, which is a narrowing. So it is a qualification, and
-- the others below are qualifications for the same reason: `stratum/2` is still
-- the stock evaluator's input, still read from derived facts, still partial in
-- the same corner, and `test/phase2.test.ts` holds all of it on that path.
amends[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_no_stratification_checker).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_reject_unstratified).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_strata_read_from_facts).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_a_stratum_order).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, l_partial_strata).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, l_unchecked_without_boot).
amends[map](d_dep_graph_is_one_tick, s_appendix_dep_edges).
amends[map](d_next_in_body_rejected, s_grammar_temporal).
amends[map](r_conclusion_tense, s_appendix_dep_edges).
amends[map](r_flows_to, s_appendix_leak).
amends[map](r_vocabulary_additions, s_vocabulary_closed).
amends[map](r_stratum_in_kernel_source, s_a_kernel_grep).

-- A QUALIFICATION is not a replacement, and the difference decides whether an
-- obligation still has to be covered. `Facts may be asserted into reserved
-- relations` narrows §2's enforcement without withdrawing it: the rule
-- rejection is still owed and still tested. Filing these three as `amends`
-- would have marked three live, tested obligations as no longer owed, which
-- is the model lying in the flattering direction.
qualifies[map](r_facts_into_reserved, s_reserved_rejected_at_load).
qualifies[map](r_unstratifiable_is_budgeted, s_reject_unstratified).
qualifies[map](r_timeless_kernel_facts, s_persistence_is_a_rule).
qualifies[map](r_edb_for_reserved, l_undefined_silenced_by_one_fact).
qualifies[map](r_moded_relations, l_demand_premise_order).

-- ---- START.md section 8 WAS REPLACED, ITEM BY ITEM, BY LIMITS.md ----------
-- `s8_out_of_scope` is ONE fact citing ONE sentence that names EIGHT things:
-- incremental maintenance, the @async executor, multi-fact abduction,
-- aggregation, GPU anything, persistence layers, optimization passes, syntax
-- sugar. A compound prohibition can only be accepted or refused WHOLE -- the
-- duty inherits the granularity of the sentence it cites -- so while three of
-- the eight had moved it could be neither covered nor honestly called open.
--
-- It does not need to be. LIMITS.md already decomposed it, and every one of the
-- eight has a mirror there, so retiring the sentence loses nothing the tree
-- still owes. That is the test `qualifies` exists for and this one passes it:
--
--   incremental maintenance -> l_no_incremental_maintenance
--   @async executor         -> l_no_async
--   multi-fact abduction    -> l_no_multi_fact_abduction
--   persistence layers      -> l_no_persistence, narrowed to
--                              `beyond store serialization` -- and `save`/`open`
--                              IS store serialization, so the persistence that
--                              was written is the permitted half, not a breach
--   aggregation, GPU,
--   optimization, sugar     -> l_no_aggregation
amends[map](l_no_incremental_maintenance, s8_out_of_scope).
amends[map](l_no_async, s8_out_of_scope).
amends[map](l_no_multi_fact_abduction, s8_out_of_scope).
amends[map](l_no_persistence, s8_out_of_scope).
amends[map](l_no_aggregation, s8_out_of_scope).

-- ...AND THE LINE THAT INHERITED THE COMPOUND NEVER CAUGHT UP. `l_no_aggregation`
-- reads `No aggregation, no optimization passes, no syntax sugar, no GPU
-- anything` and sits in the SAME FILE as eight sentences describing this
-- engine's optimizations in detail. Three quarters of it hold; the middle
-- clause is false of the tree. So it is QUALIFIED and not retired -- narrowing
-- is what the honest half deserves, and recording this as an amendment would
-- retire a prohibition on aggregation that nothing else in the tree carries.
qualifies[map](r_optimizations_exist, l_no_aggregation).

-- ---- the same obligation, written twice -----------------------------------
